  "description": "The stream of CESR-0025 in the binary domain. The size digits are unchanged (33) and now count 3-byte triplets, so the first group ends 99 bytes after its count code. The symbol legends of the Encoding Scheme Symbols Table and the indexed-code symbol table say a count code's digits determine 'the count of the following Primitives or groups of Primitives'; this case rests on the explicit rule at the Count Code tables section instead, and the conflict between the two texts is noted, not resolved, here.",
